	"subtitle": "Imhotep’s staircase to the sky",
	"history": "At Saqqara the Step Pyramid of King Djoser rose above us in six great steps, set there around 2650 BCE; why, nothing so large had ever been built of cut stone before it! Its architect, Imhotep, was so admired that later Egyptians came to worship him as a God of wisdom and healing. Having stood beneath his work, we could hardly blame them.",
